# Pairs with NoStaleAuthority. The epoch ledger pushes to and waits out every
# lease it captured, whatever membership says about the silo holding it; the
# mutant stops waiting for a silo once it is declared dead, so a silo falsely
# declared dead keeps trusting a snapshot older than a write that returned.
MODULE: DeclareFalselyDeadReleasesCapture
TARGET: NoStaleAuthority
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a false death declaration releases the advance's wait on that silo's lease
PERTURBS: DeclareFalselyDead
BOUNDS: MaxFalseDeaths = 1

--- FIND
    /\ UNCHANGED <<regVer, coveredVer, returnedVer, wstate, wsilo, owes, epoch,
                   graceOpen, graceWait, lease, pend, snapVer, scanning, knows,
                   alive, awaiting, dec, crashes, restarts, failures>>
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the advance stops waiting for the silo declared dead.
    /\ pend' = [pend EXCEPT ![s] = "no"]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<regVer, coveredVer, returnedVer, wstate, wsilo, owes, epoch,
                   graceOpen, graceWait, lease, snapVer, scanning, knows,
                   alive, awaiting, dec, crashes, restarts, failures>>
--- END
